All compilation and tests ran on the designated worker. No local Go/Rust build.
The implementation changes only the new tools/memory-probe directory and the top
Makefile's helper build, files_ephemeral copy and clean integration. Runtime,
configuration, protobuf, kernel and image-builder scripts are unchanged. Parent
module dependency pins are unchanged; x/sys v0.47.0 is selected from that module.
SquashFS remains the default; the DAX image target remains opt-in.

Actual passing checks:
- Native static build using Go 1.26.11, CGO_ENABLED=0, -trimpath and -buildvcs=false.
- Five unit tests (round trip, stat-only empty file, malformed arguments, rejection
  of invalid file mappings including FIFO, and detection of anonymous corruption).
  No skips. go vet and scoped golangci-lint both passed; gofmt was clean.
- Actual CLI stat-only on an ordinary worker filesystem file returned DAX support
  true and DAX value false, with metadata matching the fixture size.
- Two actual CLI mmap/idle/readback runs verified the selected file SHA-256 and
  full anonymous canary: a 65536-byte prefix with 2 MiB anonymous mmap and 20 ms
  idle, and the entire 221184-byte file with 2 MiB anonymous mmap and zero idle.
  All eight expected phases, monotonic timing, meminfo, rusage totals/deltas and
  positive anonymous minor faults were checked. Available DAMON maps were empty
  on this host; guest DAMON counter sampling has not been validated by this run.
- Fifteen actual CLI malformed/invalid-file cases returned nonzero with JSON
  errors, including size/duration bounds, missing/empty/non-regular paths, FIFO,
  an overlong prefix and unexpected options/positional arguments.
- ELF inspection found no interpreter. The pinned Docker builder's actual
  memory-probe-in-docker target produced bytes identical to the native build.
  Thus both checked builds have the same binary hash above.

An initial committed run at 09b196e compiled and passed unit tests/vet, but lint
reported repeated JSON keys "bytes" and "verified" (goconst). The c2f5465 correction
names these keys as constants. The initial failing log is preserved with its
hash below; all final checks were rerun from the clean corrected commit.

No guest image was built and no guest DAX, PMEM, DAMON reclaim or host-memory
improvement claim is made. Shared files_ephemeral staging supplies the probe to
standard/debug/stargz image inputs; the DAX image is derived from the same standard
rootfs. Each later actual image/guest arm must verify the installed probe hash and
run -stat-only against the file whose mapping is evaluated. Keep that file immutable
during the probe: truncation can cause SIGBUS. The probe does not drop caches,
request reclaim, lock pages, change DAMON settings or freeze other writers.
Step 3 remains WIP; its branches, dependency references and receipts are untouched.

